    ReferralDocumentUpload:
      type: object
      description: |-
        Atomic serializer for document upload + referral linking.

        Handles the complete workflow in a single API call:
        1. Validate file upload
        2. Create Document record with file
        3. Link Document to ReferralInfo via ReferralDocument
        4. Set person/family context from referral

        This reduces network round-trips and ensures data consistency.

        Trade-offs:
        - Pro: Single API call, atomic operation, better UX
        - Pro: Automatic context inheritance from referral
        - Con: More complex serializer logic
        - Con: Tightly couples upload to referral linking

        Alternative approach would be:
        1. POST to /documents/ (create Document)
        2. POST to /referrals/{id}/documents/ (link Document to Referral)

        This approach is preferred for the referral creation workflow where
        documents are uploaded as part of the consent & documents step.
      properties:
        id:
          type: string
          format: uuid
          readOnly: true
        referralInfoId:
          type: string
          format: uuid
          writeOnly: true
        referralReferenceNumber:
          type: string
          readOnly: true
        title:
          type: string
          maxLength: 255
        description:
          type: string
        documentDate:
          type: string
          format: date
          nullable: true
        file:
          type: string
          format: uri
          writeOnly: true
        categoryId:
          type: string
          format: uuid
          writeOnly: true
          nullable: true
        tagIds:
          type: array
          items:
            type: string
            format: uuid
          writeOnly: true
        isConfidential:
          type: boolean
          default: false
        isPublic:
          type: boolean
          default: false
        expiryDate:
          type: string
          format: date
          nullable: true
        notes:
          type: string
        document:
          allOf:
          - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Document'
          readOnly: true
        createdAt:
          type: string
          format: date-time
          readOnly: true
      required:
      - createdAt
      - document
      - file
      - id
      - referralInfoId
      - referralReferenceNumber
      - title
